   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "MiniMax H3 video inpaint, simple (FL2VA + DMAD 4-step, pass 1 only)\n\n1. Source video + a mask video (white = what to redraw). Same length.\n2. MAKE THE MASK BIG. H3 needs room well beyond the object, or it morphs. The Grow Mask adds 32 px on top.\n3. frame_load_cap and length must match and be 17*n + 5 (5, 22, 39 ... 141, 158, 175).\n4. Size ~1 MP (1344x768 here). Lower sizes swim and flicker more.\n5. Prompt: describe the finished shot as if it was filmed that way, not the edit.\n6. Reference picture: a still of the shot without the object (any image editor). Call it <Picture 1> in the prompt.\n   It is a big help for removals. Bypass the Load Image node if you have none.\n\nModels: minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot (FL2VA), DMAD 4-step full critic LoRA at 1.0\n(ZhengmingYu/DMAD on Hugging Face), lcm + simple, 4 steps, per the DMAD model card.\nThe FL2VA model held the redrawn area steadier than ref2va in our tests.\n\nInpaint Color Calibrate (github.com/LucianoCirino/ComfyUI-InpaintColorCalibrate) removes the slight colour cast\nH3 paints into the inpainted area. Then the original pixels are pasted back outside the mask. Original audio is kept."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "MiniMax H3 video inpaint, simple (FL2VA + DMAD 4-step, pass 1 only)\n\n1. Source video + a mask video (white = what to redraw). Same length.\n2. MAKE THE MASK BIG. H3 needs room well beyond the object, or it morphs. The Grow Mask adds 32 px on top.\n3. frame_load_cap and length must match and be 17*n + 5 (5, 22, 39 ... 141, 158, 175).\n4. Size ~1 MP (1344x768 here). Lower sizes swim and flicker more.\n5. Prompt: describe the finished shot as if it was filmed that way, not the edit.\n6. Reference picture: a still of the shot without the object (any image editor). Call it <Picture 1> in the prompt.\n   It is a big help for removals. Bypass the Load Image node if you have none.\n\nModels: minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot (FL2VA), DMAD 4-step full critic LoRA at 1.0\n(ZhengmingYu/DMAD on Hugging Face), lcm + simple, 4 steps, per the DMAD model card.\nThe FL2VA model held the redrawn area steadier than ref2va in our tests.\n\nInpaint Color Calibrate (github.com/LucianoCirino/ComfyUI-InpaintColorCalibrate) removes the slight colour cast\nH3 paints into the inpainted area. Then the original pixels are pasted back outside the mask. Original audio is kept."
   },
